rpresser wrote:
> The patch I'm thinking of would allow multiple bones files to be saved
> for each level. It would work thus:
> 
> 1) When loading a level, if there is more than one bones file for the
> level, pick one at random, with the usual chance of not loading any.
> Unlink it as usual after loading.
> 2) When the player dies, and the game has decided to save a bones
> file, if there is already a bones file saved for this level, just
> generate a new name.  (Append a letter, perhaps.)
> 
> It doesn't seem technically too difficult to implement. Is it too
> meaningless to worry about?

As far as I see, it's technically not "trivial" because you have to
implement some semaphore mechanism in multi-user environments. The
problem is in your step 1) between "When loading..." and "Unlink..."
w.r.t. the same file selected from two different Nethack processes.

Not unsolvable, not even difficult to solve, maybe, but not trivial
in the sense that you cannot just select/unlink the file in an atomic
straightforward way, and the supported platforms with their different
OS interfaces makes it not less trivial. (CMIIW.)

